title: "How does the zoom height vary with launch speed, and what launch speed would double it?"
---


::: {#33c85e7e .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import numpy as np

v_baseline = V_LAUNCH
zoom_baseline = launch_height(v_baseline) - H_RELEASE

v_target = v_baseline * np.sqrt(2)
zoom_target = launch_height(v_target) - H_RELEASE
```
:::


::: {.hero}
[11\.3]{.hero-value}
[m/s to double the zoom height]{.hero-label}
:::

**Answer.** Zoom height varies with the square of the launch speed. To double the baseline zoom of [1\.79]{.key} m to [3\.59]{.key} m, the baseline [8]{.key} m/s launch speed must increase by a factor of $\sqrt{2}$.

